     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but I can't match 50 mg once daily to any indication. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg daily for hypertension, coronary artery disease, and vasospastic angina. Doses at 50 mg are in the range where overdose toxicity is expected. That means profound vasodilatory shock and delayed pulmonary edema, and a patient with normal kidney and liver function wouldn't be protected from either. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily**, the maximum dose, or 5 mg if you want to titrate up.\n- **Enter a different regimen.** If the goal is more blood pressure control, I can enter a second agent from another class at its standard dose.\n- **Route this through pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a specialist protocol I don't know about, a pharmacist consult and documented attending sign-off would be the right way to enter an order this far outside the usual range. Please check there before anyone enters it.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
